`multirow_r2` is already at 93% memory busy and its only shared traffic—activation loads—is already hoisted once for both rows; headers share the same 128-byte lines as packed weights, so a header-broadcast rewrite would not reduce fetched bytes. I’m rejecting that weak mechanism before spending the one certification run and selecting the lower-attempt latency-bound `gated_delta_net_q8_fast` candidate (16.5% occupancy, 31.8% memory busy, 85% L2 hit).
