Hypothesis: the paired-row baseline still evaluates a uniform `have_row1` guard for every row-1 dequant block. On the production even-`M` shape that guard is always true; executing the row-1 body unconditionally (with the existing safe row-0 fallback for an odd tail) preserves every written value while shortening the scalar/control dependency chain. This is distinct from the DEAD r3 row-reuse and dual-reduction levers, and it directly tests whether control latency contributes to this low-memory-busy kernel.
