s only ONE gfx1151 (dev 1); parallel certifies would contend and corrupt measurements. For each chosen candidate i, read kernels/src/<kernel_i>.hip, write a CORRECT variant (IDENTICAL output math, SAME __global__ name+signature) to /tmp/loop_R<round>c2_i<i>.hip, then run ONE AT A TIME (NO trailing &):     SCLK=/sys/class/drm/card1/device/pp_dpm_sclk BASELINE_REF=loop_baseline_gfx1151 PREBUILT_BASE=/tmp/v2b_base_c2 RUSTUP_HOME=/home/kaden/.rustup CARGO_HOME=/home/kaden/.cargo bash /tmp/ab_certify_v2p.sh gfx1151 1 2 /home/kaden/.hipfire/models/qwen3.6-35b-a3b.mq4r <kernel_i> R<round>c2_<leverslug> /tmp/loop_R<round>c2_i<i>.hip   ab_certify_v2p ADAPTIVELY samples (4-16 A/B rounds on gfx1151, ~10-15 min each) until win-probability f resolves, and has a TOKEN-ID PARITY GATE: a variant whose greedy token-ids differ from baseline is rejected PARITY_FAIL before any A/B (this is how a coherent-but-wrong change is caught — your variant MUST be value-preserving). It auto-commits WINs to loop/card2 and logs every verdict + a per-variant profile_feedback (occ / L2-hit / mem_busy vs baseline) to the ledger.  STEP 3 -- READ the verdicts (final JSON each + the profile_feedback). Append ONE line per variant to /home/kaden/hipfire/autoresearch/state/loop_progress_gfx1151.log:     R<round>c2_<slug> kernel=<kernel> lever=<leverslug> verdict=<WIN|DEAD|INCONCLUSIVE|PARITY_FAIL|VARIANT_BUILD_FAIL> delta_pct=<d> f=<f> rounds=<n> learned=<one line, cite the profile_feedback limiter you targeted>   The lever= field FEEDS the next round's digest — make it a precise, distinct slug so you never re-derive it.  RIGOR: trust ONLY the harness verdict. WIN auto-commits to loop/card2 (rollover folds it later). INCONCLUSIVE = parked (real but unresolved at CAP) — note it, do not re-try the same lever. PARITY_FAIL / BUILD_FAIL = your variant was wrong — fix the math/signature, it does NOT count as a lever tried. Correctness before speed. Do exactly ONE round then stop.  Output a compact JSON: {"round_d